    "knowledge_point": "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{5}{x}?$",
    "worked_solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{5}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/b3a79a8dbe82342c0ab1e16371f8c1d82833f4ebc3bad659f1a619ab1e92733e.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{5}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/eeb158823a32a215dcf72d67bd27b8ad5df238ee44af535afd5850a15f9d17c0.png)",
